# November 21, 2026: South Dakota, a first scatter across the state (the emptiest state on the map that day).
# Frontier forts and a trading-post site on the Missouri, the Black Hills gold-rush towns, a sod homestead and the Cold War
# missile field by the Badlands, the Corn Palace, a double-deck river bridge, a hatchery, a sanitarium and three house museums.
# Facts come from Wikipedia (read with tools/wiki_raw.py), National Register nomination texts on NPGallery, NPS pages, HMdb
# marker texts, SD Game, Fish and Parks, the US Fish and Wildlife Service, the City of Deadwood, Deadwood History Inc., the
# Corn Palace's own page and the State Historic Preservation Office's Black Hills hikes itinerary.
